# --- Web service ---------------------------------------------------------
# Port the Express server listens on. Railway injects PORT automatically.
PORT=3000
NODE_ENV=production

# --- Shared mode: PostgreSQL + sign-in ------------------------------------
# Leave DATABASE_URL unset for the browser-only mode (no sign-in, data in
# this browser's localStorage). Set it — on Railway, reference the Postgres
# plugin as ${{Postgres.DATABASE_URL}} — and the app requires a sign-in and
# saves every change to the shared database. The tables it needs are
# created on first use. PGSSLMODE=disable is only for a local Postgres
# without TLS.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/accountingops
# PGSSLMODE=disable

# The three practice accounts are created on the first request against a
# fresh database, with these as their temporary passwords (each account must
# change it on first sign-in). An account whose variable is unset gets a
# random temporary password, logged once to stdout — set all three so it
# never has to be.
# ADNAN_TEMP_PASSWORD=
# FARHAN_TEMP_PASSWORD=
# RAYHAN_TEMP_PASSWORD=

# --- Companies House (live company lookup) ---------------------------------
# Free key from https://developer.company-information.service.gov.uk/ — read
# from server/routes/companiesHouse.mjs only, never sent to the browser. See
# docs/INTEGRATIONS.md. Without this set, onboarding falls back to a
# clearly-labelled synthetic dataset so the app still works out of the box.
# COMPANIES_HOUSE_API_KEY=

# --- Future: HMRC (Making Tax Digital) --------------------------------------
# Requires HMRC software-vendor recognition and per-client agent
# authorisation (OAuth 2.0) — not a single firm-wide key. See
# docs/INTEGRATIONS.md before assuming this can simply be filled in.
# HMRC_CLIENT_ID=
# HMRC_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Future: object storage for client documents --------------------------
# Never store client documents on the service filesystem.
# S3_BUCKET=
# S3_REGION=
# S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# --- Messaging -------------------------------------------------------------
# Email reminders are simulated (logged, not sent) unless a provider is
# chosen. Postmark: create a server at https://postmarkapp.com, verify the
# sender address or domain, then set all three. The token is read by
# server/lib/messaging/postmark.mjs only and never reaches the browser.
# MESSAGING_EMAIL_PROVIDER=postmark
# POSTMARK_SERVER_TOKEN=
# MESSAGING_FROM_EMAIL=reminders@your-practice.co.uk
# MESSAGING_FROM_NAME=Farhan & Raihan
# POSTMARK_MESSAGE_STREAM=outbound
#
# WhatsApp needs no provider: Send opens the accountant's own WhatsApp with
# the message filled in (a wa.me link). SMS stays simulated until a sender
# is chosen — see docs/INTEGRATIONS.md.

# --- Future: AI assistant ---------------------------------------------------
# The assistant only ever calls scoped tools (src/application/assistant/tools.ts).
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
